{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>This is the statute of the Torah.</b> Because the Satan and the nations of the world taunt Israel, saying: What is this commandment, and what reason is there in it? Therefore Scripture wrote of it חֻקָּה — it is a decree from before Me; you have no permission to question it (Yoma 67b)." "<b>And they shall take to you.</b> It is forever called by your name — the cow that Moses made in the wilderness." "<b>Red, without blemish.</b> That it be perfect in its redness — if two black hairs were in it, it is disqualified (Parah 2:5)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:11:35.951826266Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}